---
source: crates/standalone/fixture/src/lib.rs
---
List what is published and why, or choose what to publish.

Usage: ink select [OPTIONS] [PATHS]...

Arguments
  [PATHS]...  Pages to select, as paths in the folder: `publish: true` is
              written into the frontmatter of each, which the file must already
              have. Without a path or `--folder`, every page is listed with
              whether it is published and why

Options
      --folder <GLOB>  Select every file a glob matches (`notes/**`) by adding
                       it to `include` in ink.toml
      --remove         Take the selection back: remove `publish: true` from each
                       page, or the glob from `include`. In a public source a
                       page that is not selected is still published by default
      --dry-run        Say what would be written and write nothing

Global  -C, --json, -q, -v, --color, --no-progress, --log, --log-file
        (see `ink --help`)
More    ink select --help adds examples, notes and exit codes
